From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/common/acpi_pirq_gen: Declare the PIC _PRT with the
 entries it has

intel_write_pci_PRT() declares both packages of _PRT with map_count,
but gen_pic_route() leaves out the pins whose PIRQ is PIRQ_INVALID: on
a Lenovo ThinkCentre M920x (Cannon Point-H) the APIC branch has its 45
entries and the PIC branch 34 in a package declared 45 long, and iasl
reports "Initializer list shorter than declared package length" on the
disassembled SSDT (remark 2063). The elements past the list are
uninitialized, which an OS walking the package in PIC mode may take
for entries.

Count the pins with a PIRQ first and declare the PIC package with that
count.
---
 src/southbridge/intel/common/acpi_pirq_gen.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/common/acpi_pirq_gen.c b/src/southbridge/intel/common/acpi_pirq_gen.c
index bb0ce6f91b..ed7be72389 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/common/acpi_pirq_gen.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/common/acpi_pirq_gen.c
@@ -42,6 +42,18 @@ static void gen_pic_route(const struct slot_pin_irq_map *pin_irq_map,
 	}
 }
 
+/* The entries gen_pic_route() writes: those with a PIRQ */
+static unsigned int pic_route_count(const struct slot_pin_irq_map *pin_irq_map,
+				    unsigned int map_count)
+{
+	unsigned int count = 0;
+
+	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < map_count; i++)
+		if (pin_irq_map[i].pic_pirq != PIRQ_INVALID)
+			count++;
+	return count;
+}
+
 void intel_write_pci_PRT(const char *scope, const struct slot_pin_irq_map *pin_irq_map,
 			 unsigned int map_count, const struct pic_pirq_map *pirq_map)
 {
@@ -55,7 +67,8 @@ void intel_write_pci_PRT(const char *scope, const struct slot_pin_irq_map *pin_i
 	acpigen_pop_len(); /* package */
 	acpigen_write_else();
 	acpigen_emit_byte(RETURN_OP);
-	acpigen_write_package(map_count);
+	/* Not map_count: the pins without a PIRQ are left out below */
+	acpigen_write_package(pic_route_count(pin_irq_map, map_count));
 	gen_pic_route(pin_irq_map, map_count, pirq_map);
 	acpigen_pop_len(); /* package */
 	acpigen_pop_len(); /* else PICM */
-- 
